"""Cinematic Director: replay-powered B-roll (aerials, orbits, POV, spectate...) spliced into the edit automatically.

While Flashback (or Replay Mod) records, the creator just plays. This module turns that replay into shots:

    find_replay(slug)        which replay overlaps the OBS recording in wall-clock time
    estimate_sync / refine_sync   replay time at video t=0 (timestamps, then motion cross-correlation)
    plan_shots(slug)         choose WHERE a cinematic shot helps (transcript beats, death screens, dark/calm stretches,
                             replay events) -> projects/<slug>/broll/shots.json  (the contract, see docs/cinematic-pipeline.md)
    queue_jobs / render_queue    one job file per shot -> an Exporter backend (fake / manual / flashback_auto) -> QA
    splice_into_edl(edl, slug)   full-frame muted `video` overlays + a soft whoosh on every rendered, QA-passed shot

CLI:  mcs cinematic plan|render|status|splice|qa|sync|selftest ...      (python -m mcstudio.cinematic ... also works)
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
